SwiftNIO on Windows: apple/swift-nio#3704, "fix(windows): preserve data-path backpressure", by
mozharovsky, as of its commit 15c10a30, unchanged.
https://github.com/apple/swift-nio/pull/3704

Winsock's send, writev, recv, recvmsg and sendmsg fail with WSAEWOULDBLOCK when a nonblocking
socket can't take or give more data yet, and SwiftNIO took that for a fatal error: bulk transfers
ended in an unclean shutdown. It's now backpressure, as EAGAIN is on POSIX. It fixes issues
apple/swift-nio#3697 and #3702. Open upstream, not released yet.

